-- title:
--   Surjectivity onto the residue field passes to quotients
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ and $A$ be commutative rings with $A$ local, and let $A$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra. Let $I$ be an ideal of $A$ such that the quotient ring $A/I$ is again local (in particular $A/I$ is nontrivial, so $I \neq \top$). Assume the structure map $\mathcal{O} \to k(A)$ to the residue field of $A$, that is the composite of $\mathcal{O} \to A$ with the residue map $A \to A/\mathfrak{m}_A$, is surjective. The conclusion is that the corresponding map $\mathcal{O} \to k(A/I)$, the composite of the structure map $\mathcal{O} \to A/I$ of the quotient $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with the residue map of the local ring $A/I$, is surjective as well. Equivalently: if the residue field of $A$ is generated by the image of $\mathcal{O}$, then the same holds for the residue field of every proper quotient of $A$ that is local.
--
--   Routine bookkeeping for local $\mathcal{O}$-algebras with residue field generated by $\mathcal{O}$, the condition imposed on the test objects of a deformation problem. It is used when quotients such as $A/\mathfrak{m}^n$ are exhibited as such test objects, and is cited in the verification that the flat, ordinary and strict ordinary conditions are deformation conditions ([`GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_flatCondition`](thm.html#GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_flatCondition), [`GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_ordinaryCondition`](thm.html#GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_ordinaryCondition), [`GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_strictOrdinaryCondition`](thm.html#GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_strictOrdinaryCondition)).
